  "changelog": "0.3.5\n- Fixed: a Brain's sound now comes out of a TV or monitor connected over HDMI or DisplayPort. Before, audio was always sent to the analog headphone jack even when nothing was plugged into it, so anything playing in a Brain session was silent on an HDMI screen. This is automatic; to force a choice, set AUDIO_OUTPUT to analog or hdmi in /etc/slimeos/config. The Settings speaker and microphone tests now play through the same output.\n- Fixed: on the Remote Support and Privacy screens in Settings, the on/off box couldn't be switched by clicking the box itself (only its label text worked). The whole row is now clickable.",
